  "notes": "Event involves a Tech Spec prohibited condition (50.73(a)(2)(i)(B)) rather than equipment functional failure per se; the relief valve itself functioned as designed once repositioned. UFSAR water-seal isolation barrier and LPCI/suppression pool design context are discussed only in the Safety Analysis section as mitigating factors for safety significance, not as an operable backup system during the event window, so no BACKED_UP_BY edge was created. Previous occurrence (2019) involved a different system/type of relief valve; captured as SIMILAR_TO stub per instructions despite the narrative noting the difference, since it is explicitly referenced as a previous occurrence with a corrective-action-effectiveness link to this event."
